fontconfig memory is freed by fontconfig

FcNameUnparse returns a string the caller owns, and it was freed with free(). fontconfig here is a
NATIVE library: it allocates from the HOST allocator, so the guest free() reaches libsystem_malloc,
which does not recognise the block, reports it and ABORTS.

LIBREOFFICE FOUND IT, and only LibreOffice could have: it is the one application on the roster that
CALLS CTFontCreateForString, through
CoreTextGlyphFallbackSubstititution::FindFontSubstitute, for glyph fallback on every font preview
in its font name box. One click on Writer Document killed the process, 6 runs in 6.

  0 libsystem_c       cider_trace_abort
  1 libsystem_c       abort
  2 libsystem_malloc  malloc_vreport
  3 libsystem_malloc  malloc_report
  4 Onyx2D            O2FontPatternCoveringCharacter + 877
  5 CoreText          CTFontCreateForString + 278
  6 libvclplug_osxlo  CoreTextGlyphFallbackSubstititution::FindFontSubstitute

CORRECTING MYSELF: patch 0025 says nothing calls CTFontCreateForString and names LibreOffice as one
of the applications that does not import it. That was measured on the LAUNCHER, soffice, which is a
stub; the code lives in libvclplug_osxlo.dylib and libmergedlo.dylib, and it calls it. Check the
PLUGIN dylibs, not the executable, before saying an application does not use something.

FcStrFree is the fontconfig free and uses the same allocator.
--- a/Onyx2D/O2Font_freetype.m
+++ b/Onyx2D/O2Font_freetype.m
@@ -253,7 +253,12 @@
 
                 if (unparsed != NULL) {
                     answer = [NSString stringWithUTF8String: (const char *) unparsed];
-                    free(unparsed);
+                    /* FcStrFree, NOT free. fontconfig is a NATIVE library here and allocates from
+                     * the host allocator, so handing its pointer to the guest free() reaches
+                     * libsystem_malloc, which reports it and ABORTS. LibreOffice found this the
+                     * hard way: it calls CTFontCreateForString for glyph fallback on every font
+                     * preview, and one click on Writer Document killed it (#217). */
+                    FcStrFree(unparsed);
                 }
             }
             FcPatternDestroy(match);
